Subject: [PATCH] player: make FILL mode scale uniformly instead of stretching

"填充" (FILL) previously mapped to Modifier.fillMaxSize(), which forces the
video GLSurfaceView to exactly the screen size. The video is drawn to fill
the view, so on displays that are not 16:9 the picture is stretched
non-uniformly (on a 3:2 screen a 16:9 video is squashed sideways / stretched
vertically).

Make FILL use the same algorithm as the existing CROP mode: fill the height,
then let aspectRatio pick the width from the real video ratio. AspectRatio
falls back to an aspect-correct size that may exceed the incoming max width
(the z=false attempts), so the view becomes wider than the screen and gets
cropped at the edges - i.e. a uniform zoom ("cover") instead of a stretch.

Before:
    :cond_1b                  # ordinal 1 = FILL
    move v3, v6                # v6 = 1.0f
    invoke-static {v2, v3}, Lsj7;->c(Ld15;F)Ld15;   # fillMaxSize(1.0f)
    move-result-object v6

After:
    :cond_1b
    invoke-static {v2, v6}, Lsj7;->e(Ld15;F)Ld15;   # fillMaxHeight(1.0f)
    move-result-object v3
    invoke-virtual/range {v17 .. v17}, Llm7;->r()F   # state.aspectRatio
    move-result v6
    invoke-static {v3, v6, v4}, Lva0;->R(Ld15;FZ)Ld15;  # aspectRatio(ratio)
    move-result-object v6

Obfuscated Compose layout helpers in this build:
    Lsj7;->c  = fillMaxSize        (FillElement, Both)
    Lsj7;->e  = fillMaxHeight      (FillElement, Vertical)
    Lsj7;->b  = fillMaxWidth       (FillElement, Horizontal)
    Lva0;->R  = aspectRatio(ratio, matchHeightConstraintsFirst)
